# scripts/*.patch are real git-diff output, applied verbatim with `git apply` (see
# scripts/install_geoml.cmake/install_adgeoml.sh) - a unified diff's own exact byte
# content, including its line endings, is part of what it describes, so Windows
# checkouts' default core.autocrlf=true LF->CRLF conversion corrupts it, causing
# `git apply` to fail with "corrupt patch at <file>:<line>" (confirmed directly:
# this is what broke scripts/geoml-occt79-compat.patch on windows-latest CI).
# Marking these -text disables line-ending conversion entirely, on any platform.
scripts/*.patch -text
